WEBVTT

00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:05.040
A query returning one order does not prove that the reader inspected one row.

00:00:05.040 --> 00:00:08.945
Iceberg first uses metadata to choose candidate files.

00:00:08.945 --> 00:00:12.320
Rows in a kept file can still fail the row filter.

00:00:13.820 --> 00:00:18.445
The fixture has three batches with disjoint order identifier ranges.

00:00:18.445 --> 00:00:25.295
For order one thousand and five, the ranges zero to thirty nine and two thousand to two thousand and thirty nine cannot match.

00:00:25.295 --> 00:00:29.220
Only the range one thousand to one thousand and thirty nine is kept.

00:00:30.720 --> 00:00:35.890
The remaining file contains forty candidate records, but only one row matches.

00:00:35.890 --> 00:00:37.970
These are different quantities.

00:00:37.970 --> 00:00:42.540
Selected file bytes are a sum of file sizes, not measured network traffic.

00:00:42.540 --> 00:00:49.050
Run the experiment with an Iceberg row filter, then change the target to a value outside every range.
